        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c1_makes_three_contributions_first_intr",
          "text": "The paper makes three contributions. First, it introduces LightSB, a lightweight solver that combines two recent ideas: parameterizing the Schrödinger potential with sum-exp quadratic, that is Gaussian mixture, functions, and viewing the log-potential as an energy function.",
